To find the average amortization expense from 2006 to 2008, I will use the amortization expenses for each year provided in the document. The relevant information is:

- Amortization expense for 2008: $90 million
- Amortization expense for 2007: $77 million
- Amortization expense for 2006: $64 million

The formula for the average is the sum of the values divided by the number of values. In this case, it is (90 + 77 + 64) / 3.

Now, I will calculate the average using the calculate tool.
```json
{
  "message": "Calculating the average amortization expense from 2006 to 2008.",
  "tool": "calculate",
  "arguments": {
    "expression": "(90 + 77 + 64) / 3"
  }
}
```